The 'services-server' folder contains the backend server implementation for the Shattered Archive project, managing API endpoints and business logic. It serves as the core runtime environment that handles client requests and data processing, forming the backbone of the application's functionality. The folder includes TypeScript configuration files that enable proper compilation and dependency management for the Node.js server. It is also the shared home for auth-introspect-client.ts (Phase 2 centralized auth service) — the Ed25519 assertion-signing + POST /api/introspect helper any Node consumer (mud-builder-server, and future web-server/game-server/kingdom-tactics-server) uses to validate a token against auth-server.
